ng  very fast here again I'm sped it up  about 20 times so you can you can  imagine just how long this takes I am  NOT the fastest of typers and I make  frequent errors as well that have to be  gone back over and corrected but when  I'm finished for any given video that  I'm going to shoot I've got you know  anywhere from 10 to 20 slides and I'm  ready to use those for the video  since I'm using my chalkboard in all of  these videos and since I don't have time  as I'm lecturing to write all this stuff  down I try to put as much as I can on  the board before I actually go to film  the video and you can see me I'm  referring to the text you know this  these half-hour Haegele videos are very  intensive as far as the amount of  thinking that has to go into how to  represent things schematically it's  quite a challenge but you can see me  here gradually working out one of the  paragraphs and writing all the stuff  that I'm going to need for that  particular lecture up on the board after  that It's Showtime  I need to set up the camera the lighting  and get myself ready for for filming in  front of the chalkboard again I'm going  to speed this up really quick you see me  put my jacket and go to town you know I  take a little pause before I begin  sometimes I have to do multiple takes  particularly if there's a lot of outside  noise or if I lose my train of thought  which occasionally does happen you can  see that little tiny video camera  recording me up there that's what I use  I use a tripod and a flip cam and some  decent lighting and that's pretty much  it last step as far as video production  is the editing and that is a pretty  laborious process as well there's a lot  of stuff you can see me gradually  working on the video here you're going  to see more and more Clips being added  to it over time I see me right there  adding in some of the slides and now I  have to scroll up and find the  recordings of when I actually read the  text which happened a long time ago and  cut and paste each of those sections you  know adding some features to them if I  need to some sound and things like that  then I build the text itself as you can  see me doing here into each of the  reading sections and then we're getting  close  to being finished there's a bit of  review because as I've learned you can  never check a video enough times to  catch all of the typos and possible  little errors in it that is it that's  the video process if you have any  questions about it go ahead and leave  them in the comments and I'll answer  them there so thanks to everybody for  watching and sharing and commenting on  the videos and thanks in particular to  my patreon supporters
 

